# Forever scoring (every class)

Item facts come from Wowhead Forever ingest. All nine classes are on this model. Re-score one class at a time after a rule change. Do not `reemit_all.py` from stale JSON.

**Order:** damage (spec primary) first, then survivability (sta/armor below 60), then endurance (mana keep-up, less than stam). Level 60 is raw raid weights. Max 3 unique names + 1 notable per slot.

## Do not change weights unless asked

`weights.json`, the numbers in `score.py` `weights_at_level()`, and `ScoringWeights.generated.lua` stay until the user explicitly asks for a retune. A piece ranking first because of an existing weight is the model working.

Priest, mage, and warlock `dpsWeightRanged` is **7** (same scale as a warrior melee weapon). These classes cast, then wand. **White Obsidian Wand** (274425) is rank 1 ranged at 39 for mage, priest, and warlock because 7 × 41.47 DPS wins the slot. Do not lower that weight to bury it. Greater Magic Wand stays the client 17.5 DPS. Warlock schools and Enhancement Tank armor (0.20, 0.40 below 60) stay as they are.

Holy paladin levels in melee. Shown below 60: healing, spell power, and holy spell power **1.8**, intellect **1.2**, spirit **1.5** (Reverence), mana per 5 **2.2**, flat mana **0.08**, crit **0.8**, armor **0.15**. `+Holy Spell Damage` is stored as `spHoly` and must stay equal to generic spell power. Cloth `armorClass` is **0.62**, mail **0.96**, plate **1.0**. Do not put intellect back above healing, and do not flatten the cloth penalty so tailoring robes outrank blacksmithing mail and plate healing.

## Coordinates, sets, tooltips, scrapes

- A hunt gets a coordinate whenever a real spot exists (quest start, dungeon or raid entrance, named creature, vendor, object). Do not invent one. A quest reward pin is where the **first** quest in that chain begins, the step that leads to the item. Walk the Wowhead series to that first quest and pin its start. A later step's giver is where you continue, not the pin. If that first step starts inside a dungeon, pin the dungeon entrance. Heavehammer begins at Lost Relic Carry (Alliance) and Elder Knowledge (Horde), both at the Excavation Site entrance in the Wetlands (47.8, 56.3), not at the turn-in. Rage of the Storm and the other Tempest's Weapons rewards begin at Call of Air: Alliance Ironforge 46.2, 13.0 (quest 94789), Horde Orgrimmar 37.4, 37.2 (1531) and Thunder Bluff 24.2, 20.4 (1532). The Horde series on Wowhead starts at Elemental Aid (Rau Cliffrunner, Thousand Needles); that is the next giver, not the pin. A generic world drop (no named creature) filed under one faction's zone stays on both lists. Through level 15 each faction gets one pin already published on its own side (`GENERIC_LOW_FARM`: Elwynn 48.2, 42.8 and Durotar 42.0, 68.4 for 1–7; Westfall 31.0, 46.2 and Barrens 51.0, 29.4 for 8–15). Above 15 both factions share the catalog spot, with no faction tag. Do not invent a coordinate. A named creature in that zone stays on that faction's list. Unsourced has none until a source exists. Ruins of Lordaeron is Undercity map 1458 at 71.6, 11.4. Patch with `index_coordinates.py --ids`. Do not full-emit (`emit()` rewrites the whole file).
- Hunter ranged is Bow, Gun, and Crossbow only. Thrown does not fire Auto Shot. Rogue and warrior still list thrown weapons. Beast Mastery and Marksmanship melee `dpsWeight` is **0.05**. Their strength is **0**. That leaves **Armor of the Fang** off their chest list: the chest has no agility, and the 5-piece stun is priced at 0.05, so legs, feet, belt, and gloves stay the hunt from 18 through about 24 and the chest does not. Do not force the chest back unless asked. Survival strength is **0.7**, and Survival melee stays **10**. Survival keeps all five Viper pieces through 23. Ranged stays **14** for Beast Mastery and Marksmanship, and **6** for Survival. Feral keeps all five through 23 because the stun uses 14 plus 1 point. Do not drop that point. The log shows hunters a **Two-hand** block, then a **Main hand** block of main-hand-only weapons, then an **Off Hand** slot. Main-hand weapons stay in that list. The Off Hand character panel bar shows either-hand weapons only (tooltip One-Hand), because a main-hand weapon cannot be equipped there. The Main Hand paper-doll slot is the two-hand list. The Off Hand paper-doll slot is the either-hand list. Enhancement shows **Two-hand** only. No one-hand list and no off-hand list. Rogue **Main Hand** is tooltip Main Hand only. Rogue **Off Hand** is One-Hand and Off Hand. An either-hand weapon does not sit under the Main Hand header.
- Every re-score counts set bonuses (Embrace of the Viper, Rotmender's Raiment, any `(N) Set`) via `apply_embrace_package` / `apply_rotmender_package`. Pieces scored alone are the wrong list.
- Tooltip layout stays Wowhead line order. Slot and type are one double line, and so are Damage and Speed. The client set is spliced in place. Drop Chance, Requires Level, and Sell Price stay in the tail. If the stored tip already has `(N) Set`, do not add the client set again. Random-suffix greens keep the jackpot tooltip.
- A generic dungeon or raid mob is `raid_trash`. The log labels that source **Dungeon & Raid trash**. **Gloves of the Fang** drop from **Druid of the Fang**, not from a Wailing Caverns boss. A named boss stays `boss_drop`. Wowhead's boss flag is missing on real bosses, so a missing flag is not trash. A rare that is not in `bossNpcs` is `rare_npc`.
- A Wowhead Forever scrape **inserts new ids only**. Do not refresh existing `items.json` facts from the tooltip cache (that reverted Erudite to a stale blue). Then recheck every item still marked Unsourced: if the listview or tooltip now names a quest, a vendor, or Dropped by, fill that source and `index_coordinates.py --ids` those ids. Do not call a still-empty row a world drop.
- Every newly indexed item is checked for Wowhead's **New in Forever** badge in the same pass. The test is a classic nether tooltip 404 (`https://nether.wowhead.com/classic/tooltip/item/{id}`), not `id >= 200000`. Season of Discovery items in that range still exist on classic and stay unstamped. Run `python pipeline/scripts/build_forever_new.py`. It only probes ids missing from `pipeline/data/forever_wowhead/new_in_forever.json` and rewrites `GearQuest/_generated/Data.ForeverNew.generated.lua`. The parchment stamp is the burnt Forever mark beside the reward. Hover text is "New in Forever".

## Random-enchant jackpot is BiS

Rank a random-enchant green on the **best suffix it can roll** (top of that suffix’s range), not the expected value across every suffix.

- Superior Shoulders of Agility at 22 is **+6–7 Agi** (~9.5%). If that roll would be #1 in the slot, it **must** appear as BiS #1.
- `suffixChance` / the log hint tell the player the roll is slim. Chance never buries the hunt.
- Implemented in `pipeline/scripts/score.py` `best_variant` (`ROLL_POLICY="bestRoll"` ranks on jackpot).

## Leveling survivability (below 60)

Leveling is not raid min-max. Stamina, health, and armor beat a naked +1 primary-stat upgrade.

- Example: at 22, **Brawler’s / Trapper’s Leather Tunic** (8 Agi + stam / str / int) beat **Panther Armor** (9 Agi, no stam).
- `score.py` `weights_at_level()` multiplies sta / health / hp5 ×3 and armor ×2 when `level < 60`.

## Leveling endurance (below 60)

Survivability also means having and keeping mana. Call this **endurance**. It is less important than stamina, but it matters for most classes (paladin seals/heals, shaman shocks, hunter shots, caster drinks).

- `weights_at_level()` multiplies int / spirit / mp5 / mana ×2 when `level < 60` (stam is ×3).
- Level 60 uses the raw raid-scale weights. Forever level-60 guides may pin later; until then `GQ_NO_GUIDES=1`.

## Warrior tank is physical

Warrior Protection does not score spell power or healing. A glove with +SP / +healing (Silvered Gauntlets) is not BiS even if the stam is fat. If it also has defense, it is the **notable** for that slot — not rank 1.

## Shaman Enhancement Tank is a hybrid

Like paladin Protection: 1h + shield, stamina/armor/defense first, then Rockbiter melee threat, then Earth Shock / Lightning Shield spell threat. Not dual-wield (Forever has no shaman DW). `enhancement_tank` in `weights.json`.

## Refreshed Forever tooltips (score from these)

Stored item facts must match the refreshed Wowhead Forever tooltip before a score. `refresh_forever_tips.py` writes those facts, then re-score. Do not score a row that still disagrees with the tooltip. Do not full-ingest to refresh tips (that replaces `sources.json` for id ≥ 200000). The 7 Oct 2026 pass updated 1186 items from nether tips and then re-scored all nine classes. Client pins stay: Coldflame, Silverlaine, Wolfsbane required level 20. Kaleidoscope resist 5 stays. Emit the audit **before** rescoring so recovered ids leave `FOREVER_MISSING`.

- The Equip line `Increases damage and healing done by magical spells and effects by up to N` is stored as **both** heal=N and damageDone=N. Do not strip it. Do not collapse it to spell power only. `forever_stats` folds damageDone into spell power so it is not counted twice. Holy uses the heal half. Mages (heal weight 0) use the damage half. An unequal "healing up to X and damage up to Y" stays heal=X, damageDone=Y (Staff of Westfall: 48 and 16). Skip party lines. A green `+N Spell Power` line is spell power only.
- **Required level is the tooltip `Requires Level`, never item level.** A stated level greater than 1 is never replaced. Fang of Magmatus is 13. Every item with **no** required level (or Wowhead's stub of 1) is assumed to be a quest reward, or some other gated source, until looked up. Find the quest on Wowhead Forever and set the required level to the **minimum** level that can pick up that quest (`Requires level N`; item XML `<json>` reqlevel, not `jsonEquip`, not the scaling minLevel). Several quests: take the lowest. A chain of at least five steps that must enter a dungeon uses that step's quest level when it is at least 8 levels above the pickup. Final Passage (Windstorm Hammer 6804, Dancing Flame 6806) is 36 because Test of Lore in Scarlet Monastery Library is level 36. Mage's Wand (7513, 7514, 11263) is 40 because Rituals of Power is level 40. Confront Yeh'kinya (20218, 20219) is 58. Drakefire Amulet (16309) is 60. Leaders of the Fang stays 10. The Defias Brotherhood stays 14. The item-level floor is only a stand-in until that lookup is done. Fang is not pinned over Golemheart.
- Cloaks, rings, necks, trinkets, and held items with `kind` `?` are `Misc`. `kind` `?` is not equippable.
- Weapon headers are labels only. If a staff is rank 1, main-hand rank 2 is the one-hand that off-hand rank 1 pairs with. A second staff may sit at rank 3 with a higher score than rank 2.
- Fishing and skinning are Profession. A crafted hunt states the Forever recipe skill on the line just before Source. The skill clause is green when the character meets the recipe and red when they are short or do not have the profession. The description does not repeat it: strip `Crafted with Leatherworking (requires skill N).` and list recipe materials there (`Materials: Light Leather (8), Coarse Thread (4).`) from the Wowhead Forever spell tooltip via `fetch_craft_skills.py --reagents`. Every new profession hunt, and every update of an existing profession hunt, looks that skill up in the same pass: ForeverDB `made` on `crafting/{id % 64}.json`, confirmed on the Wowhead Forever spell page (`Requires Leatherworking (40)`) when Wowhead is up. The item tooltip does not carry it. Run `fetch_craft_skills.py`. A skill of 1 is real when both say 1. Do not invent 1. Dress Shoes (6836) has no recipe. Container loot uses the Container filter. Boss drop has a dungeon flyout for the dungeons that have a boss-drop hunt at the current level, including lower ranks. Dungeon & Raid trash has the same flyout for trash hunts at the current level, and those boxes are separate from Boss drop. Hall of Thanes, Ruins of Lordaeron, and Excavation Site are on that list. Other is bosses that are not in a dungeon or raid. The flyouts do not scroll. Select all / Deselect all on the filter menu covers the source list and the profession, boss, and trash sub-filters. Play style sits at the bottom of the log. Five cards, names under the pictures, three then two. The green upgrade arrow is on both lists. It stays on the unfiltered best pieces when a filter or a play style hides them, and it stays on every hunt still showing, including a later rank, a notable, or a tracked hunt. Get it now can be on with either dungeon card, and with Don't look back and Buy it. No Dungeons and Dungeon Enjoyer turn each other off. Don't look back hides a hunt once its required level would be a gray quest (GetQuestGreenRange on the live character). Buy it keeps vendor pieces and anything that is not bind on pickup, unless a vendor sells that bind on pickup piece. No Dungeons hides hunts that send you into a dungeon or raid, including a quest that enters one at any step. A world drop stays even when its zone is a dungeon or raid name, or the pin is that entrance. Captain Melrache's Cape stays. World bosses and crafts you can buy stay. Dungeon Enjoyer keeps only those dungeon and raid hunts, so world bosses, crafts, vendors, and outdoor hunts stay hidden. Get it now hides a hunt until this character meets the standing stored on that item, or can make a bind-on-pickup craft. A bind-on-equip craft stays unless the item itself requires the profession to wear. Reaching the standing or the skill shows the hunt without turning the style off. An active filter hides source types that have no checkbox. The parchment shows `Rank #N` in a black box above the item title, using the stored slot rank (`curatedRank`), so a filtered or play-style list still shows the real rank. Hovering the box says best, 2nd, 3rd, or 4th in that slot for a hunt on the unfiltered list. A hunt that only appears because a filter, a play style, or both are on gets the same line from its stored rank, plus which of those is on. `GetItemInfo` names of the form `Item 23173` are not names; use the stored fact or audit name.

## Mage Battle Mage

Caster who swings. Specs: `battlemage_frost` (the hunt), `battlemage_fire`, `battlemage_arcane`. Spell power of that school first. Stamina base 0.15 (slightly above frost 0.1). Weapon `dpsWeight` 0.35. Coldflame Saber and Blade of Silverlaine stats are the Forever **client** tooltip, pinned in `client_item_overrides.json`. Do not sync the Wowhead nether tip back over them. The saber’s 98 Fire vs Frozen is every swing during a freeze (`FROZEN_MELEE_UPTIME` 25% frost, 15% fire/arcane). On an imbued weapon, printed stats stay the normal colors and only the imbue effect is grey. Do not repeat that effect. Add `Use: Combine the <base weapon> and <scroll>.` (`CLIENT_IMBUE` in `Data.lua`).
